#Serverless Static Website Hosting on AWS

## Project Overview
This project demonstrates how to host a static website using a serverless architecture on Amazon Web Services (AWS).  
The website is deployed using Amazon S3 for storage, CloudFront for global content delivery, and Route 53 for custom domain management.  
This setup ensures scalability, high availability, low cost, and enhanced security with HTTPS (SSL).

---

## Features
- Serverless architecture with no manual server management  
- Static website hosting using Amazon S3  
- Global content delivery using Amazon CloudFront  
- Optional custom domain mapping via Amazon Route 53  
- HTTPS-enabled security using AWS Certificate Manager (ACM)  
- Cost-effective and highly available web hosting solution  

---

