## Step-by-Step Deployment Guide

### Step 1: Create an S3 Bucket
1. Open the AWS Management Console and go to S3.  
2. Click "Create Bucket" and give it a unique name (e.g., my-serverless-website).  
3. Uncheck "Block all public access".  
4. In the Properties tab, enable "Static Website Hosting".  
5. Upload your website files (index.html, style.css, script.js, etc.).  
6. Set the index document as `index.html`.

---

### Step 2: Configure Bucket Policy
To allow public access to your website files, apply the following bucket policy  
(Replace `my-serverless-website` with your bucket name):

```json
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Sid": "PublicReadGetObject",
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Principal": "*",
      "Action": "s3:GetObject",
      "Resource": "arn:aws:s3:::my-serverless-website/*"
    }
  ]
}
Step 3: Set Up CloudFront Distribution
Open CloudFront and create a new distribution.

Select your S3 bucket as the origin.

Choose "Redirect HTTP to HTTPS" under Viewer Protocol Policy.

Attach a custom SSL certificate from AWS Certificate Manager (optional).

Save the distribution and note the CloudFront domain name (e.g., d123abcd.cloudfront.net).

Step 4: Configure Route 53 (Optional)
In Route 53, create a new Hosted Zone for your domain.

Create an A record (Alias) pointing to your CloudFront distribution.

Once propagated, your website will be available at your domain name.

Step 5: Secure with HTTPS
Open AWS Certificate Manager (ACM) in the us-east-1 (N. Virginia) region.

Request a Public Certificate for your domain name.

Validate using DNS validation (Route 53 can do this automatically).

Once issued, attach the certificate to your CloudFront distribution.

Step 6: Clear CloudFront Cache
After making updates to your website:

Go to CloudFront → Invalidations → Create Invalidation.

Enter /* and confirm to clear cached content.

Output
Public S3 URL: http://my-serverless-website.s3-website-us-east-1.amazonaws.com

CloudFront URL: https://d123abcd.cloudfront.net

Custom Domain (optional): https://www.myserverlesswebsite.com

Benefits
High availability and fault tolerance

Global distribution with minimal latency

Free SSL certificate via ACM

Scalable and pay-as-you-go pricing

Simplified deployment and maintenance

